#: ../../upstream/docs/user/user-defined-redirects.rst:28
msgid "Built-in redirects"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/user-defined-redirects.rst:30
msgid ""
"This section explains the redirects that are automatically active for all"
" projects and how they are useful. Built-in redirects are especially "
"useful for creating and sharing incoming links, which is discussed in "
"depth in :doc:`/guides/best-practice/links`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/user-defined-redirects.rst:37
msgid "Page redirects at ``/page/``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/user-defined-redirects.rst:39
msgid ""
"You can link to a specific page and have it redirect to your default "
"version, allowing you to create links on external sources that are always"
" up to date. This is done with the ``/page/`` URL prefix."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/user-defined-redirects.rst:43
msgid ""
"For instance, you can reach the page you are reading now by going to "
"https://docs.readthedocs.io/page/guides/best-practice/links.html."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/user-defined-redirects.rst:45
msgid ""
"Another way to handle this is the ``latest`` version. You can set your "
"``latest`` version to a specific version and just always link to "
"``latest``. You can reach this page by going to "
"https://docs.readthedocs.io/en/latest/guides/best-practice/links.html."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/user-defined-redirects.rst:52
msgid "Root URL redirect at ``/``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/user-defined-redirects.rst:54
msgid ""
"A link to the root of your documentation (`<slug>.readthedocs.io/`) will "
"redirect to the  :term:`default version`, as set in your project "
"settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/user-defined-redirects.rst:57
msgid ""
"This works for both readthedocs.io (|org_brand|), readthedocs-hosted.com "
"(|com_brand|), and :doc:`custom domains </custom-domains>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/user-defined-redirects.rst:59
msgid "For example::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/user-defined-redirects.rst:65
msgid ""
"You cannot use the root redirect to reference specific pages. ``/`` "
"*only* redirects to the default version, whereas ``/some/page.html`` will"
" *not* redirect to ``/en/latest/some/page.html``. Instead, use "
":ref:`page_redirects`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/user-defined-redirects.rst:70
msgid ""
"You can choose which is the :term:`default version` for Read the Docs to "
"display. This usually corresponds to the most recent official release "
"from your project."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/user-defined-redirects.rst:74
msgid "Root language redirect at ``/<lang>/``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/user-defined-redirects.rst:76
msgid ""
"A link to the root language of your documentation "
"(``<slug>.readthedocs.io/en/``) will redirect to the  :term:`default "
"version` of that language."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/user-defined-redirects.rst:79
msgid ""
"For example, accessing the English language of the project will redirect "
"you to the its default version (``stable``)::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/user-defined-redirects.rst:84
msgid "Shortlink with ``https://<slug>.rtfd.io``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/user-defined-redirects.rst:86
msgid ""
"Links to ``rtfd.io`` are treated the same way as ``readthedocs.io``. They"
" are intended to be easy and short for people to type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/user-defined-redirects.rst:89
msgid "You can reach these docs at https://docs.rtfd.io."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/user-defined-redirects.rst:95
msgid "User-defined redirects"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/user-defined-redirects.rst:98
msgid "Page redirects"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/user-defined-redirects.rst:100
msgid ""
"*Page Redirects* let you redirect a page across all versions of your "
"documentation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/user-defined-redirects.rst:104
msgid ""
"Since page redirects apply to all versions of a project, ``From URL`` "
"doesn't need to include the ``/<language>/<version>`` prefix (for "
"example, ``/en/latest``), only the path to the page. Page redirects don't"
" apply to translations or subprojects, which need their own redirect "
"rules. If you need a redirect for a specific language or version URL, use"
" :ref:`user-defined-redirects:exact redirects` with the fully-specified "
"path."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/user-defined-redirects.rst:113
msgid "Exact redirects"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/user-defined-redirects.rst:115
msgid ""
"*Exact Redirects* take into account the full URL (including language and "
"version), allowing you to create a redirect for a specific version or "
"language of your documentation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/user-defined-redirects.rst:119
msgid "Clean/HTML URLs redirects"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/user-defined-redirects.rst:121
msgid ""
"If you decide to change the style of the URLs of your documentation, you "
"can use *Clean URL to HTML* or *HTML to clean URL* redirects to redirect "
"users to the new URL style."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/user-defined-redirects.rst:124
msgid ""
"For example, if a previous page was at ``/en/latest/install.html``, and "
"now is served at ``/en/latest/install/``, or vice versa, users will be "
"redirected to the new URL."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/user-defined-redirects.rst:129
msgid "Limitations and observations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/user-defined-redirects.rst:131
msgid ""
"|org_brand| users are limited to 100 redirects per project, and "
"|com_brand| users have a number of redirects limited by their plan."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/user-defined-redirects.rst:133
msgid ""
"By default, redirects only apply on pages that don't exist. **Forced "
"redirects** allow you to apply redirects on existing pages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/user-defined-redirects.rst:135
msgid ""
"Redirects aren't applied on :doc:`previews of pull requests </pull-"
"requests>`. You should treat these domains as ephemeral and not rely on "
"them for user-facing content."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/user-defined-redirects.rst:137
msgid ""
"You can redirect to URLs outside Read the Docs, just include the protocol"
" in ``To URL``, e.g ``https://example.com``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/user-defined-redirects.rst:139
msgid ""
"A wildcard can be used at the end of ``From URL`` (suffix wildcard) to "
"redirect all pages matching a prefix. Prefix and infix wildcards are not "
"supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/user-defined-redirects.rst:141
msgid ""
"If a wildcard is used in ``From URL``, the part of the URL that matches "
"the wildcard can be used in ``To URL`` with the ``:splat`` placeholder."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/user-defined-redirects.rst:143
msgid ""
"Redirects without a wildcard match paths with or without a trailing "
"slash, e.g. ``/install`` matches ``/install`` and ``/install/``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/user-defined-redirects.rst:145
msgid ""
"The order of redirects matters. If multiple redirects match the same URL,"
" the first one will be applied. The order of redirects :ref:`can be "
"changed from your project's dashboard <guides/redirects:Changing the "
"order of redirects>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/user-defined-redirects.rst:149
msgid ""
"If an infinite redirect is detected, a 404 error will be returned, and no"
" other redirects will be applied."
msgstr ""

