#: ../../upstream/docs/user/user-defined-redirects.rst:241
msgid "Redirecting a page to the latest version"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/user-defined-redirects.rst:243
msgid ""
"Say you want your users to always be redirected to the latest version of "
"a page, your security policy (``/security.html``) for example. You can "
"use a wildcard with a forced redirect to redirect all versions of that "
"page to the latest version::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/user-defined-redirects.rst:254
msgid ""
"From ``https://docs.example.com/en/v1.0/security.html`` to "
"``https://docs.example.com/en/latest/security.html``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/user-defined-redirects.rst:256
msgid ""
"From ``https://docs.example.com/en/v2.5/security.html`` to "
"``https://docs.example.com/en/latest/security.html``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/user-defined-redirects.rst:261
msgid ""
"``To URL`` includes the domain, this is required, otherwise the redirect "
"will be relative to the current version, resulting in a redirect to "
"``https://docs.example.com/en/v1.0/en/latest/security.html``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/user-defined-redirects.rst:266
msgid "Redirecting an old version to a new one"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/user-defined-redirects.rst:268
msgid ""
"Let's say that you want to redirect your readers of your version ``2.0`` "
"of your documentation under ``/en/2.0/`` because it's deprecated, to the "
"newest ``3.0`` version of it at ``/en/3.0/``. You can use an exact "
"redirect to do so::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/user-defined-redirects.rst:278
msgid ""
"From ``https://docs.example.com/en/2.0/dev/install.html`` to "
"``https://docs.example.com/en/3.0/dev/install.html``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/user-defined-redirects.rst:283
msgid ""
"For this redirect to work, your old version must be disabled, if the "
"version is still active, you can use the ``Force Redirect`` option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/user-defined-redirects.rst:287
msgid "Creating a shortlink"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/user-defined-redirects.rst:289
msgid ""
"Say you want to redirect ``https://docs.example.com/security`` to "
"``https://docs.example.com/en/latest/security.html``, so it's easier to "
"share the link to the page. You can create a redirect with the following "
"configuration::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/user-defined-redirects.rst:299
msgid ""
"From ``https://docs.example.com/security`` (no trailing slash) to "
"``https://docs.example.com/en/latest/security.html``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/user-defined-redirects.rst:301
msgid ""
"From ``https://docs.example.com/security/`` (trailing slash) to "
"``https://docs.example.com/en/latest/security.html``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/user-defined-redirects.rst:305
msgid "Migrating your docs to Read the Docs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/user-defined-redirects.rst:307
msgid ""
"Say that you previously had your docs hosted at "
"``https://docs.example.com/dev/``, and choose to migrate to Read the Docs"
" with support for multiple versions and translations. Your documentation "
"will now be served at ``https://docs.example.com/en/latest/``, but your "
"users may have bookmarks saved with the old URL structure, for example "
"``https://docs.example.com/dev/install.html``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/user-defined-redirects.rst:312
msgid ""
"You can use an exact redirect with a wildcard to redirect all pages from "
"the old URL structure to the new one::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/user-defined-redirects.rst:320
msgid ""
"From ``https://docs.example.com/dev/install.html`` to "
"``https://docs.example.com/en/latest/install.html``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/user-defined-redirects.rst:324
msgid "Migrating your documentation to another domain"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/user-defined-redirects.rst:326
msgid ""
"You can use an exact redirect with the force option to migrate your "
"documentation to another domain, for example::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/user-defined-redirects.rst:336
msgid ""
"From ``https://docs.example.com/en/latest/install.html`` to "
"``https://newdocs.example.com/en/latest/install.html``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/user-defined-redirects.rst:340
msgid "Changing your Sphinx builder from ``html`` to ``dirhtml``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/user-defined-redirects.rst:342
msgid ""
"When you change your Sphinx builder from ``html`` to ``dirhtml``, all "
"your URLs will change from ``/page.html`` to ``/page/``. You can create a"
" redirect of type ``HTML to clean URL`` to redirect all your old URLs to "
"the new style."
msgstr ""

